WEBVTT

00:00:06.889 --> 00:00:09.457
[ sighs]

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:15.898
[ soft buzzing]

00:00:17.682 --> 00:00:22.252
[ squeaking]

00:00:26.778 --> 00:00:31.261
[ creaking]

00:00:36.353 --> 00:00:38.137
[ rustling]

00:00:38.181 --> 00:00:41.401
[ panting]

00:00:41.445 --> 00:00:45.231
[ wind whistling]

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:47.886
[ barking]

00:00:48.887 --> 00:00:53.370
[ horn blowing]

00:00:59.594 --> 00:01:01.552
[ brakes squeal and whoosh]

00:01:01.596 --> 00:01:03.119
"Welcome to the Knight Bus,

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:06.339
"emergency transport for the
stranded witch or wizard.

00:01:06.383 --> 00:01:08.864
"My name is Stan Shunpike

00:01:08.907 --> 00:01:12.781
and I will be your conductor
for this evening."

00:01:15.784 --> 00:01:17.742
What you doin' down there?

00:01:17.786 --> 00:01:19.048
I fell over.

00:01:19.091 --> 00:01:20.397
What'd you fell over for?

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:22.225
I didn't do it on purpose.

00:01:22.268 --> 00:01:23.400
Well, come on, then.

00:01:23.443 --> 00:01:26.359
Let's not wait for
the grass to grow.

00:01:32.627 --> 00:01:34.977
What you lookin' at?

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:35.804
Nothing.

00:01:35.847 --> 00:01:37.327
Well, come on, then.

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:41.070
In. Nah, nah, nah.
I'll get this. You get in.

00:01:41.113 --> 00:01:43.942
[ grunts]

00:01:45.291 --> 00:01:47.990
Gordon Bennett.
[ groans]

00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:51.384
[ snoring]

00:01:55.563 --> 00:01:57.434
[ tinkling]

00:01:57.477 --> 00:01:58.653
SHUNPIKE:
Come on. Move on.

00:01:58.696 --> 00:02:00.742
Move on, move on.

00:02:00.785 --> 00:02:02.265
[ exhales]

00:02:02.308 --> 00:02:04.093
[ sniffs]

00:02:04.136 --> 00:02:05.790
[ clears throat]

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:07.966
[ bell dings]

00:02:08.793 --> 00:02:11.709
[ exhales]

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:16.714
Take 'er away, Ern.

00:02:16.758 --> 00:02:17.889
Yeah...

00:02:17.933 --> 00:02:19.848
Take it away, Ernie.
It's going to be

00:02:19.891 --> 00:02:21.110
a bumpy ride!

00:02:21.153 --> 00:02:23.286
[ cackling]

00:02:26.506 --> 00:02:29.118
[ chandelier tinkling]

00:02:31.163 --> 00:02:33.775
What did you say
your name was again?

00:02:33.818 --> 00:02:34.993
I didn't.

00:02:35.037 --> 00:02:36.647
Well, whereabouts
are you 'eaded?

00:02:36.691 --> 00:02:39.824
The Leaky Cauldron.
That's in London.

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:41.043
Did you 'ear that, Ern?

00:02:41.086 --> 00:02:42.653
The Leaky Cauldron.
That's in London.

00:02:42.697 --> 00:02:44.089
SHRUNKEN HEAD:
The Leaky Cauldron.

00:02:44.133 --> 00:02:45.525
Hey, if they have the pea soup,

00:02:45.569 --> 00:02:46.962
make sure you eat it
before it eats you.

00:02:47.005 --> 00:02:50.443
[ cackling laugh]

00:02:51.531 --> 00:02:52.837
HARRY:
But the Muggles!

00:02:52.881 --> 00:02:53.838
Can't they see us?!

00:02:53.882 --> 00:02:54.839
SHUNPIKE:
Muggles?!

00:02:54.883 --> 00:02:56.232
They don't see nothin', do they?

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:57.102
SHRUNKEN HEAD:
No, but if you jab them

00:02:57.146 --> 00:02:58.974
with a fork they feel!

00:02:59.017 --> 00:03:00.410
[ laughing]

00:03:00.453 --> 00:03:03.369
Ernie, little old lady
at twelve o'clock!

00:03:06.721 --> 00:03:08.331
[ yells] Oof!

00:03:08.374 --> 00:03:12.030
[ heavy breathing]

00:03:12.074 --> 00:03:15.033
SHRUNKEN HEAD:
Ten, nine, eight,

00:03:15.077 --> 00:03:17.949
seven, six, five, four,

00:03:17.993 --> 00:03:20.343
three, three-and-a-half...

00:03:20.386 --> 00:03:22.737
two, one-and-three-quarters...

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:24.608
Yes!

00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:29.787
HARRY:
Who is that?

00:03:29.831 --> 00:03:31.659
That man.

00:03:31.702 --> 00:03:34.183
[ sighs]

00:03:34.226 --> 00:03:36.185
Who is that?

00:03:36.228 --> 00:03:38.013
Who is...?

00:03:38.056 --> 00:03:40.450
That is Sirius Black, that is.

00:03:40.493 --> 00:03:43.235
Don't tell me you've
never been 'earing

00:03:43.279 --> 00:03:44.715
of Sirius Black.

00:03:44.759 --> 00:03:47.326
He's a murderer.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:50.939
Got 'imself locked up
in Azkaban for it.

00:03:50.982 --> 00:03:52.288
How did he escape?

00:03:52.331 --> 00:03:54.812
Well, that's the
question, isn't it?

00:03:54.856 --> 00:03:56.684
He's the first
one that done it!

00:03:56.727 --> 00:04:02.515
He was a big supporter of...
you-know-who.

00:04:02.559 --> 00:04:05.388
Reckon you've
'eard of 'im.

00:04:05.431 --> 00:04:09.261
Yeah.
Him I've heard of.

00:04:10.785 --> 00:04:13.788
Ernie, two double-deckers
at twelve o'clock.

00:04:13.831 --> 00:04:15.877
They're getting closer, Ernie.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:19.141
Ernie, they're right
on top of us!

00:04:25.887 --> 00:04:28.454
Mind your head.

00:04:28.498 --> 00:04:32.458
[ laughing]

00:04:33.372 --> 00:04:37.376
Hey, guys! Guys!
Why the long faces?

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:39.117
[ laughing]

00:04:44.253 --> 00:04:45.820
Yeah! Yeah!
Nearly there. Nearly there.

00:04:45.863 --> 00:04:47.256
Nearly there.

00:04:47.299 --> 00:04:48.953
[ Harry yells]

00:04:49.388 --> 00:04:51.739
[ car alarm blaring]

00:04:51.782 --> 00:04:53.175
The Leaky Cauldron.

00:04:53.218 --> 00:04:55.177
SHRUNKEN HEAD:
Next stop, Knockturn Alley.

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:59.137
Ah... Mr. Potter... at last.

00:04:59.181 --> 00:05:01.226
[ car alarm blaring]

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:02.662
SHUNPIKE:
Take 'er away, Ern!

00:05:02.706 --> 00:05:05.665
SHRUNKEN HEAD:
Yeah, take it away, Ernie!

00:05:06.971 --> 00:05:11.062
[ car alarm blaring]

00:05:13.369 --> 00:05:15.806
[ alarm chirps off]

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:20.071
[ low and indistinct chatter]

